---
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { t, prefix, type Lang } from '../i18n';
interface Props { lang: Lang }
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const c = t(lang);
const mail = SITE.contactEmail;
---
<article class="legal wrap narrow">
  {lang === 'zh' ? (
    <Fragment>
      <h1>使用条款</h1>
      <div class="draft-banner" role="note"><strong>{c.legal.draft}</strong><br />{c.legal.draftBody}</div>
      <p class="muted small">{c.legal.updated}：2026-10-07</p>

      <h2>1. 开源软件</h2>
      <p>千剪 Reelfold（桌面应用、video-studio 技能和本网站）免费，按 MIT 许可开源（见仓库中的 LICENSE）。软件按现状提供，不附带任何形式的担保；桌面应用目前是预览版，功能可能变化。</p>

      <h2>2. 你的责任</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>你对素材拥有使用权，并已得到画面中其他人（嘉宾、学员）对出镜和声音使用的同意；没有同意的部分，请遮挡或删除。</li>
        <li>你自己发布视频，并遵守各平台的规则，包括按要求标注 AI 生成或 AI 处理过的内容。千剪只帮你填写发布内容，不会替你点发布。</li>
        <li>你使用第三方 AI 服务（Claude Code、Codex、各家 API 或模型）时，需要遵守对应服务商的条款，费用由你和服务商结算。</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. AI 处理的局限</h2>
      <p>剪辑、字幕和文案由 AI 生成并经过自动检查，但仍可能有错，例如字幕听错词。发布前请自己看一遍。</p>

      <h2>4. 第三方组件</h2>
      <p>字体、模型和其他第三方组件遵循各自的许可（例如 SIL OFL 1.1、Apache-2.0），详见仓库中的许可说明。</p>

      <h2>5. 联系</h2>
      <p>问题和建议请在 GitHub 上提 issue 或参与讨论，也可以发邮件到 <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>。</p>
      <p><a href={`${prefix(lang)}/`}>{c.legal.back}</a></p>
    </Fragment>
  ) : (
    <div lang={lang === 'fr' ? 'en' : undefined}>
      {lang === 'fr' && <p class="draft-banner" lang="fr" role="note">Cette page n’est disponible qu’en anglais pour le moment.</p>}
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <div class="draft-banner" role="note"><strong>{c.legal.draft}</strong><br />{c.legal.draftBody}</div>
      <p class="muted small">{c.legal.updated}: 2026-10-07</p>

      <h2>1. Open-source software</h2>
      <p>Reelfold (the desktop app, the video-studio skill and this website) is free and open source under the MIT licence (see LICENSE in the repository). It is provided as is, without warranty of any kind; the desktop app is a preview and may change.</p>

      <h2>2. Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You have the rights to your footage and the consent of other people in it (guests, students) to use their face and voice; where you do not, mask or remove them.</li>
        <li>You publish the videos yourself and follow each platform’s rules, including labelling AI-generated or AI-edited content where required. Reelfold fills in the post; it never presses publish for you.</li>
        <li>When you use third-party AI services (Claude Code, Codex, any API or model), you follow their terms and settle any fees with them.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Limits of AI processing</h2>
      <p>Edits, captions and copy are produced by AI and checked automatically, but may still contain errors such as misheard caption words. Please watch before posting.</p>

      <h2>4. Third-party components</h2>
      <p>Fonts, models and other third-party components keep their own licences (for example SIL OFL 1.1 and Apache-2.0); see the licence notes in the repository.</p>

      <h2>5. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions and suggestions: open an issue or a discussion on GitHub, or email <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>.</p>
      <p><a href={`${prefix(lang)}/`}>{c.legal.back}</a></p>
    </div>
  )}
</article>
